course: dictionary
lesson: 3854
title: Four: one word, more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «A satnav or phone finds its position by timing radio signals from at least four satellites in orbit.» Here four is the number 4, one more than three.
explain: Four can also be a digit, the written sign 4. «Hyphens join all the parts of one number: quatre-vingt-huit is one number, 88, not four separate numbers.» In this sentence, the hyphens show that the parts make one number, so four is not being used to count separate things.
explain: Context can also point to a meaning that has nothing to do with numbers. «On all fours» means on hands and knees, so a child crawling on the floor is on all fours. Check by swapping your meaning into the sentence: does «at least four satellites» still make sense if four means hands and knees? No, so the number meaning is right.
fact: Four is the number 4, one more than three.
fact: A four is the digit 4, the written sign for the number.
fact: «On all fours» means on hands and knees.
fact: Four is used in all four operations: add, subtract, multiply and divide.
fact: In maths, a square has four sides, and a rectangle has four corners.
exercise: «A satnav finds its position by timing radio signals from at least four satellites.» What does four mean here? | A written letter | On hands and knees | *The number 4 | A tree with leaves
exercise: Lee writes «the puppy was on all fours». What does on all fours mean? | Four o'clock in the afternoon | Four very fast horses | A four-leaf clover | *On hands and knees
exercise: «Four coders who each fix 12 bugs a day fix 4 × 12 = 48 bugs a day.» Which operation is 4 × 12? | *Multiplication | Subtraction | Division | Addition
test: How many sides does a square have? | Three | Six | *Four | Two
test: What does the hyphen show in «quatre-vingt-huit»? | That it is a sum to add | That it is a word for a letter | That four separate numbers are here | *That all the parts make one number
exam: In «on all fours», is four a number? | *No, the phrase means on hands and knees | Yes, it is a sum | Yes, it is the number 4 | Yes, it is the digit 4
